hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23323","Rawh narrated to us, Ali ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: Uyayna ibn Badr, al-Aqra' ibn Habis, and Alqama ibn Ulatha gathered at the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they mentioned lineages, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you wish, I will tell you: The forefather of Banu Amir is a red or dusky camel eating from the edges of the trees. He said: And I think he said: In a meadow. And Ghatafan is a rough hill driving the people from it. He said: So al-Aqra' ibn Habis said: Then where is the forefather of Banu Tamim. He said: Had he kept silent."
